This project provides a scalable, affordable, and customizable assistive technology platform to foster inclusive learning environments. By transforming written text into real-time spoken audio, the system bridges critical learning gaps, increases classroom engagement, and improves the overall academic performance and social integration of disabled students in resource-limited settings.
## 💡 Key Applications

* 📰 Accessible Reading: Reading newspapers, textbooks, and captions.
* 💊 Daily Assistance: Interpreting medicine labels and navigational signs.
* 🏫 Special Education: Providing an affordable desktop learning model for classrooms.

------------------------------
## 🎯 Project Objectives## 1. Hardware Setup & Configuration

* Seamless Integration: Link peripherals (Webcam, Speakers, Display) with the Raspberry Pi 4.
* Stable Deployment: Maintain system integrity using specialized 5V power supply configurations.
* Operating System: Utilize standard Linux-based Raspberry Pi OS (Raspbian) environments.

## 2. Core Functionality

* Optical Image Capture: Capture physical documents using a USB Webcam.
* Text-to-Speech (TTS): Convert extracted text characters into clear audio speech.
* Multi-Channel Audio: Deliver output via HDMI, 3.5mm audio jacks, or external USB speakers.

------------------------------
## 🛠️ System Architecture & Hardware
The platform leverages the computational power of the Raspberry Pi 4 Single-Board Computer alongside standard peripheral devices.

       [ USB Webcam ] --------> ( Captures Text Image )

                                       |
                                       v
 [ Power Supply (5V) ] ----> [ Raspberry Pi 4 ] <--- [ Keyboard & Mouse ]
 (Micro-USB/Type-C)          (Broadcom BCM2711)
                                       |
                                       v
                               [ Audio / Video ]
                               /               \
                              v                 v
                 [ Monitor / Display ]     [ USB Speakers / Headphones ]

## 🎛️ Component Breakdown

* SoC: Broadcom BCM2711 Quad-core ARM Cortex-A72 processor.
* Memory: 2GB to 8GB RAM options (allocates temporary execution data).
* Storage: MicroSD Card pre-loaded with Raspberry Pi OS.
* Peripherals: High-speed USB 3.0/2.0 ports for webcams, keyboards, and audio peripherals.
* Connectivity: Gigabit Ethernet, Built-in Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth modules.

------------------------------
## 🚀 Getting Started & Setup## 🔌 Hardware Connections

   1. Plug the USB Webcam into one of the blue USB 3.0 ports on the Raspberry Pi 4.
   2. Connect your USB Speakers or Headphones into an available USB or 3.5mm audio port.
   3. Connect your Monitor using an HDMI-compatible cable to the micro-HDMI port.
   4. Hook up your USB Keyboard and Mouse.
   5. Insert the pre-configured MicroSD card and attach the 5V Power Supply.

## 💻 Software Implementation Checklist

Note: This section can be updated with your exact script names (e.g., Python scripts using OCR engines like Tesseract and TTS engines like gTTS/Espeak).


* Ensure your Raspberry Pi OS environment is fully updated:

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

* Configure the default audio driver settings to output speech through your preferred device (HDMI or USB/3.5mm Jack).

